  "question": {
    "text": "A rigid nitrogen tank stored inside a laboratory has a pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math> atm at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>06</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>00</mn></math>&nbsp;am when the temperature is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>03</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>00</mn><mi>pm</mi></math>, when the temperature is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, the pressure in the tank will be _____ atm. [nearest integer]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "32",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to Gay Lussac law At constant volume and mole</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>30</mn><mn>300</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>318</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>30</mn><mn>300</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>318</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>32</mn></math></p>",
